1
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:26,880
Aiming for the evening sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:34,000
I kicked a whetstone and
even my shoes flew off,

3
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:42,300
onto the head of a carpenter
who was chopping away.

4
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:48,460
They laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if I pass my energy on to others,
it's Katsushika, after all.

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,540
With a yawn, the unchanging
streets feel strangely gentle.

7
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:14,580
From the pointed-hat water tower,
up toward the great sky,

8
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:16,780
the sun sets.

9
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:25,280
Tomorrow, too,
it all ends like this, doesn't it.

10
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:30,400
Katsushika, Shibamata, even happiness lost,

11
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,840
because I'm a fool who finally realized.

12
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:41,000
A talk that's not even a talk.

13
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:41,240
Talk.

14
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:46,300
Everyone, I got us some juice!

15
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:48,320
Wow, bottled juice!

16
00:01:48,940 --> 00:01:51,100
Bottled drinks are rare these days,
aren't they?

17
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:54,240
Yeah, lately it's all cans and PET bottles.

18
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:56,180
Glass bottles are mostly useless now.

19
00:01:56,180 --> 00:01:59,600
Right? I found them at the liquor store
and just couldn't resist buying them.

20
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:01,660
That's right, Sen-nuki, Sen-nuki!

21
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:04,140
He gets strangely excited whenever something like this comes up,
doesn't he?

22
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:08,060
This is bad, we don't have a Sen-nuki!

23
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:11,640
Oh no, we can't open
them without a Sen-nuki.

24
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:14,820
We don't use Sen-nuki anymore these days,
you know.

25
00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:18,260
Who needs a Sen-nuki?
You just pull it out like this.

26
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:23,780
Unbelievable.

27
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:25,180
Your teeth don't break

28
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:30,480
My teeth have been strong since I was a kid,
so this is nothing.

29
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:34,740
I have the record for opening six
dozen beer bottles in one minute!

30
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:37,140
Six dozen? That's seventy-two bottles!

31
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:39,540
I made a bet with your big brother.

32
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:43,120
When money's involved,
Ryo-chan will do anything, won't he?

33
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,200
Honestly.

34
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:45,200
What?

35
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:48,500
Then I'll give you all yours for free.

36
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,780
Reiko, lend me a hand for a sec.

37
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:03,980
Awful!

38
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:05,940
The diamond's split in half!

39
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:08,760
W-what terrifying teeth!

40
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:11,380
My teeth can do much more than this!

41
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:12,620
On the phone

42
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:14,120
Locker

43
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,100
Helmet

44
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:17,280
Now

45
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,120
How about that?

46
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:28,080
Now do you see how strong my teeth are?

47
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:30,000
Aaaaaah!

48
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,120
Aaaaaah!

49
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,360
Aaaaaah!

50
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:33,860
Aaaaaah!

51
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:34,360
Aaaaaah!

52
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:47,840
Imagine

53
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:49,660
What on earth is all this commotion?

54
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:52,520
Chief, my front tooth...

55
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:55,300
What? Your front tooth is missing!

56
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:56,800
It fell out.

57
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:00,120
Do that much,
and even teeth have their limits.

58
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:04,620
You probably did something reckless
again and ended up in this mess.

59
00:04:04,620 --> 00:04:06,200
Serves you right.

60
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:06,660
But, you know...

61
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:09,880
Your front tooth was lying right here.

62
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:11,400
Damn it!

63
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:13,520
Losing a tooth over something so trivial,
you wimp!

64
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:15,100
You spineless tooth!

65
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:16,420
This

66
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:17,900
That's enough, senpai.

67
00:04:18,380 --> 00:04:20,560
You should go to the dentist right away.

68
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:25,240
I'm proud that I've never once
been to a dentist since I was born!

69
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:27,340
That's not something to be proud of.

70
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:29,480
Just go to the dentist already.

71
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:33,120
But treating a front tooth might cost a lot

72
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:33,980
Yeah.

73
00:04:33,980 --> 00:04:37,380
If you get a ceramic tooth,
you'd better be ready to pay 100,000 yen.

74
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:39,760
100,000?

75
00:04:39,940 --> 00:04:42,200
One front tooth for 100,000 yen?!

76
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:44,540
No way.

77
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:46,720
I'll just glue it back on with super glue.

78
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:48,580
Teeth are basically like plastic.

79
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:51,480
If you stick it snugly to the teeth on both sides,
it'll go right back in place.

80
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:53,700
What an incredible way to fix it.

81
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:55,560
Right?

82
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:56,480
Come on.

83
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:58,160
Found it, here it is.

84
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,500
The blood got stuck to my tooth.

85
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:10,160
You idiot! What have you done?!

86
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:14,040
You'd better take that tooth out quickly,
Ryo-san.

87
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:16,680
I'll take it out for you, so come over here.

88
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:17,720
Please.

89
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:21,440
It's pretty hard, isn't it.

90
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:22,120
Hey.

91
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:23,720
It hurts!

92
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:26,480
No way, another tooth came out with it too!

93
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:28,640
What?!

94
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:30,240
Ouch, that really hurt.

95
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:33,320
Decide now, then glue it back in.

96
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:36,600
This time, for sure.

97
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:46,960
Ended up sticking it
in the wrong spot again.

98
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:51,460
Why do so many trucks have
to pass by today of all days!

99
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:55,800
Senpai, I'll grab it this time.

100
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,300
Alright. Go ahead.

101
00:05:57,300 --> 00:06:01,360
In the end, four of them came out.

102
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:05,140
Ryotsu, before it's too late to undo,

103
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:06,400
why don't you go see a dentist?

104
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:09,140
Chief, if they treat four teeth,

105
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:11,220
how much money do you think that'll cost?

106
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:14,180
Or are you going to pay
for the treatment, Chief?

107
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:16,760
Why should I have to go that far?!

108
00:06:17,260 --> 00:06:20,460
Even without four teeth,
I can get by just fine like this.

109
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,200
You never know.

110
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:25,060
The rest of your teeth might
all fall out at once, too.

111
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:27,780
Like an overworked person
who suddenly drops dead.

112
00:06:27,780 --> 00:06:29,860
Reiko, don't scare me like that.

113
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:33,480
Ryo-san, you've been taking advantage
of your strong health until now,

114
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:35,580
and you hardly brushed your teeth, did you?

115
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:37,280
That's not true.

116
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:40,440
I brush my teeth properly about once a month,
you know!

117
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:42,220
Normally, you brush them every day.

118
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:46,020
With you, Senpai,
your nutrition balance is a total mess too.

119
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:48,160
If you do that,
maybe your teeth will get better.

120
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:49,380
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

121
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:53,660
What should I eat for a good nutritional
balance to make my teeth strong?

122
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,100
Foods rich in calcium.

123
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:58,000
Like small dried sardines
or tiny dried anchovies.

124
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,140
I've got calcium tablets, if that helps.

125
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:01,740
Then feed them to me!

126
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:03,780
It's not too late, even now.

127
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:11,880
It has no flavor at all. It's awful.

128
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,340
Drinking it all at once like that!

129
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:16,880
More importantly, senpai,
brushing your teeth matters more.

130
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:18,860
Yeah, I'll give you that.

131
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:22,300
Uh-oh, my toothbrush is gone!

132
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:24,860
Ryo-chan, you never had one to begin with.

133
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:26,660
This will do.

134
00:07:30,780 --> 00:07:32,760
Hey, don't be so wasteful!

135
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,580
Then this will do.

136
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:38,520
Just think of it as a big toothbrush.

137
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:45,060
Ryotsu! W-that's the toilet cleaning brush!

138
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:49,400
Why would anyone leave
it in a place like this?

139
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:50,360
Idiot!

140
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:51,920
Ryo-chan...

141
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:55,220
S-senpai, if you don't mind,
please use mine.

142
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:57,160
It's too late for that now!

143
00:07:57,220 --> 00:08:00,500
Never mind!
The Credor might work well for polishing it!

144
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:01,920
I can't bear to watch.

145
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:03,360
Ryo-chan, don't die.

146
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:07,560
Now what?

147
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:12,680
Another tooth's come out too!

148
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:18,360
Yep, that's Ryo-chan.

149
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:20,420
He looks like Uncle Reredere.

150
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:26,640
Idiot! Can't you even take the shortcut?

151
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:28,520
What the hell are you doing?!

152
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:29,780
I can't wait any longer!

153
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:32,580
Ryo-chan, the traffic has stopped moving.

154
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:42,020
I won't mess up again.

155
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:44,260
Senpai, aren't you done yet?

156
00:08:44,260 --> 00:08:50,120
Ryotsu, hurry up already!

157
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:56,980
Hurry, Ryo-chan!

158
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:58,200
Senpai!

159
00:08:58,740 --> 00:09:00,040
Ryotsu!

160
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:05,800
Ryotsu!

161
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,440
Did you do it, Ryotsu?

162
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,320
Ryo-chan!

163
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:09,200
Senpai...

164
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:18,340
Eh?

165
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:21,020
Ryotsu, your mouth isn't open.

166
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:26,200
You used too much glue, and your
upper and lower teeth stuck together.

167
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:29,420
Let's go upstairs.

168
00:09:29,420 --> 00:09:30,280
Here you go, Ryo-chan.

169
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:32,720
Come on, Mamoru-kun,
it's time for your greeting.

170
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:36,160
I'm allowed to greet them?
Is that really okay? Is it okay?

171
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:37,820
Huh?

172
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:41,720
No! Don't pull such a corny, lame bit!

173
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:43,700
Sorry!

174
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:56,140
My, my teeth...

175
00:09:56,140 --> 00:10:03,560
My teeth...

176
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:04,860
My teeth...

177
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:07,640
Be careful, senpai!

178
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:10,780
Why are my teeth...

179
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,697
My...

180
00:10:18,747 --> 00:10:21,780
My, my teeth...

181
00:10:21,780 --> 00:10:24,220
Looks like we have no choice
but to make you dentures.

182
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:27,140
No way, dentures are expensive and awful.

183
00:10:27,140 --> 00:10:31,400
If I'm spending 400,000 yen on teeth, I'd rather
make them myself out of plastic model kits.

184
00:10:31,980 --> 00:10:32,980
Ryotsu

185
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:35,100
Go ahead.

186
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:38,860
They say when people get old,
they fall apart starting with their teeth.

187
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:44,000
No matter how much stamina you have,
you're a full-fledged old man now.

188
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:49,180
I really wanted my teeth to grow back.

189
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:52,400
Senpai, I'll ask a dentist I know

190
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:55,940
to make that kind of bridge for you cheaply.

191
00:10:55,940 --> 00:10:59,740
On Respect-for-the-Aged Day,
I'll take good care of you.

192
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:00,760
Ryotsu-kun

193
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:09,940
What? Liver isn't needed anymore?

194
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:13,040
When I had him looked
at by a dentist I know,

195
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,280
they were all baby teeth.

196
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:16,300
What?

197
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:19,720
So senpai is going to grow
permanent teeth from now on.

198
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:21,400
One by one.

199
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:23,280
Gently, gently.

200
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:24,000
Yeah, yeah.

201
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:28,440
Normally, children switch from baby teeth to
permanent teeth in elementary school, right?

202
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:30,120
When I asked senpai,

203
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:33,280
he said he doesn't remember
losing a single tooth until now.

204
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:37,340
So Ryotsu has been getting by
on baby teeth this whole time?

205
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:39,300
Looks that way.

206
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:40,780
Chief.

207
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:42,700
Ryo-chan is just so cute, you know.

208
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:43,420
Look,

209
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:44,440
look, look!

210
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:47,180
Well, this is...

211
00:11:47,180 --> 00:11:48,540
Quite...

212
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:49,860
What adorable little teeth!

213
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,740
They only just came in this morning!

214
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:53,680
Aren't they cute, like a baby's teeth!

215
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:54,120
Right?

216
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:55,490
Honestly,

217
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:58,900
Not only is his head childish,
his teeth are too!

218
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:03,746
You lot,

219
00:12:03,796 --> 00:12:07,380
once your new teeth come in,
I'll let you pull them out!

220
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:11,300
Take good care of your
new teeth this time, Ryotsu!

221
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:17,140
Ryo-san, you're going to be fine!

222
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:23,940
I don't know how, but I've won a prize.

223
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:27,240
It must be because I've
always been such a good person.

224
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:28,953
Well then,

225
00:12:29,003 --> 00:12:31,800
the address should be around here...

226
00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:41,240
Here it is.
I've got a bad feeling about this.

227
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:43,580
Hellooo!

228
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:48,720
Just as I thought.

229
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:57,240
Russian tea drunk while
doing the Cossack dance

230
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:59,000
tastes like Terestroika.

231
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,760
A man who knows the difference,
Kosuke Ezaki!

232
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:03,820
It's you again, Professor Ezaki.

233
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:05,760
Long time no see, Gorilla-kun.

234
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,120
After England, France, and China,

235
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:10,440
when did you become a Russian Kaburo?

236
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:14,420
Ahaha! Ever since I saw it on TV last week!

237
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:19,180
On TV? Did you summon me all this
way just to show off that creepy dance?

238
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:21,850
Nyeh! Wrong, Gorilla-kun.

239
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:24,560
You're going to the moon with me.

240
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:26,420
The moon?!

241
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:33,160
W-what, something like this
in the bathhouse chimney!?

242
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:35,080
So then, Gorilla-kun,

243
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:38,940
you should have the courage of

244
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:42,600
Laika, the dog who boarded a satellite
for the former Soviet space program.

245
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:45,540
What courage is there in forcing
a dog that doesn't want to go?

246
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:49,640
Why on earth do I have to take such
a risk and go to the Moon anyway?

247
00:13:50,020 --> 00:13:54,820
It's been kept secret until now, but the
Moon holds an enormous amount of diamonds.

248
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:56,540
Diamonds?

249
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:59,660
The many craters on the Moon's surface,

250
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:02,300
what do you think caused them?

251
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:05,083
Long ago, the Moon's craters

252
00:14:05,133 --> 00:14:07,600
were formed by meteorites crashing down.

253
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:10,097
And because of the
enormous pressure from that,

254
00:14:10,147 --> 00:14:14,320
vast amounts of diamonds lie
sleeping within the Moon's strata.

255
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:20,460
Let's do it, Professor.
Space is humanity's love and romance.

256
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:24,300
Yo, sweeper, sweeper.
Thank you, Gorilla-kun.

257
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:26,995
With this, you too, Mohri-san, Mukai-san,

258
00:14:27,045 --> 00:14:30,120
following Wakata-san, will be the
second Japanese person to fly into space.

259
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:31,820
Ha ha ha ha

260
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:35,980
Oops, I forgot Gachapin and Akiyama-san.

261
00:14:36,380 --> 00:14:38,280
Once that's decided, let's go right away!

262
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:40,800
Roger! They say
"Strike while the iron's hot!"

263
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:43,200
Alright, we're all set!

264
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:50,420
Alright, launch!

265
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:53,340
Hey, wait! I'm not even in my seat yet!

266
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:01,140
Amazing cheetah.

267
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:03,220
Gorilla-kun, you held on well, didn't you.

268
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:07,520
It's dangerous to leave your seat, you know.

269
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:09,020
You're the dangerous one.

270
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:19,680
Third-stage separation.

271
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:24,520
What was that just now?

272
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:27,540
It's nothing.

273
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:29,880
Anyway, how about it?

274
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:31,620
A moment of silence, then a toast.

275
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:33,320
That's a thoughtful touch.

276
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:35,720
But when it's in a tube,

277
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:37,800
it's like juice from a corner candy shop.

278
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:38,960
Cheers!

279
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:45,760
Could this be vodka?

280
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:48,060
That's not right.

281
00:15:48,060 --> 00:15:49,080
It's vodka.

282
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:52,760
Hey, you can't even drink yet and
you're knocking back strong liquor!

283
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:54,300
I feel great.

284
00:15:54,300 --> 00:15:57,220
Hey, don't throw up here!
We're in zero gravity!

285
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:02,620
Harasshaa, we've reached the Moon!

286
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:05,020
As fast as a manga, impressive as always.

287
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:07,980
We have to hurry and get to work.

288
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:11,640
Let's take a commemorative photo
with the Earth in the background.

289
00:16:11,640 --> 00:16:15,320
Garira-kun, we didn't come here
on a sightseeing trip, you know.

290
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:17,780
Fine, I'll take it myself then.

291
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:20,940
Wait, I want to be in it too.

292
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:25,140
Alright, next we'll take one
in front of the landing module.

293
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:31,360
Well, we've taken the photos,
so it's about time to

294
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:32,300
head back, I suppose.

295
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:35,880
Hey, you're joking, right?

296
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:38,480
We came all the way to the Moon
just to take a commemorative photo!

297
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:42,720
We accidentally jettisoned the
extra oxygen and fuel earlier.

298
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:44,760
Only the fuel for the return trip is left.

299
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:45,800
What?

300
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:51,920
So that's what that "da" was

301
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:53,960
So that "da" was it, huh

302
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:55,500
Yeah, that "da" was it

303
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:57,980
That "da" risked his
life to get to the Moon,

304
00:16:57,980 --> 00:17:01,200
and now he has to go home without achieving his goal.
That was the "da."

305
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:04,780
Yeah, we wasted our precious remaining
time taking commemorative photos,

306
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:08,140
and now we have no time left to dig for the diamonds.
That was the "da"!

307
00:17:08,140 --> 00:17:09,460
Five minutes left

308
00:17:10,080 --> 00:17:11,160
What's that voice?

309
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,360
It's the computer!

310
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:15,480
We flew manually on the way here,
but the way back is on autopilot.

311
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:16,100
That's right!

312
00:17:16,100 --> 00:17:20,120
Damn it! Damn it!
There's no way I'm going home empty-handed!

313
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:21,020
Gorilla-kun!

314
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:24,680
Diamonds! Diamonds! Diamonds! Diamonds!

315
00:17:24,740 --> 00:17:26,440
Gorilla-kun! We're out of time!

316
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:28,120
Three minutes left!

317
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:30,560
Hey! There are only three minutes left!

318
00:17:30,660 --> 00:17:34,560
Shut up! If no diamonds turn up,
I'm burying you right here and going home!

319
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:39,580
What's wrong, Gorilla-kun?

320
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:41,800
I found some strange rock!

321
00:17:42,260 --> 00:17:42,580
What?

322
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:45,960
This is...

323
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:50,300
genuine diamonds!

324
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:53,280
We did it!
There really were diamonds on the Moon!

325
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:55,880
I was right after all.

326
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:58,120
Alright, let's find even more!

327
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:03,260
Oh no, is it time to leave already?

328
00:18:03,260 --> 00:18:05,380
No, it's teatime.

329
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:05,780
Hey.

330
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:08,060
Don't do things that
confuse people like that.

331
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:10,700
I am the seagull.

332
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:11,220
You

333
00:18:11,270 --> 00:18:15,260
Russian tea while gazing at the
distant Earth is still something special.

334
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:19,680
It reminds me of the dawn over Moscow
I saw from the Trans-Siberian Railway!

335
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:22,240
Y-you only saw it on TV, didn't you?

336
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:26,180
What is it, is it teatime again?

337
00:18:26,900 --> 00:18:29,120
Oh no! Gorilla-kun, it's the departure bell!

338
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:33,200
What?! Damn it, they used a misleading bell!

339
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:36,000
Hurry, hurry, Gorilla-kun!

340
00:18:38,380 --> 00:18:40,280
There's a huge diamond
in a place like this -

341
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:48,400
Even with one-sixth of Earth's gravity,
it's still pretty heavy.

342
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,200
It's departure time!

343
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:51,560
Ignite the engines!

344
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:52,580
Garira-kun!

345
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:56,080
Wait!

346
00:18:56,080 --> 00:18:58,760
No good, it's on autopilot!

347
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:00,660
Hey, close the hatch!

348
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:02,500
Don't leave me behind!

349
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:06,760
Even if we get yelled at, it's too late now.

350
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:11,640
Oh no, how are we supposed to get back now?

351
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:18,060
Well, never mind. We can think
about how to get back to Earth later.

352
00:19:20,080 --> 00:19:22,940
Wait, you left Senpai on the Moon?

353
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:28,080
He was searching for diamonds until
the last minute and missed the rocket.

354
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:30,700
But did you really go to the Moon?

355
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:33,120
See for yourself.

356
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:36,400
It's true, they really took photos.

357
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,540
That idiot.

358
00:19:37,540 --> 00:19:38,680
Ryo-chan...

359
00:19:39,260 --> 00:19:42,140
I'm worried, since we left him there alone.

360
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:44,040
No need to worry.

361
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:46,780
Professor, Ryotsu is very resourceful.

362
00:19:46,780 --> 00:19:48,800
He can get by anywhere.

363
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:50,000
R-really?

364
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:54,340
I have a feeling that gorilla-kun
of ours will manage somehow too.

365
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,440
Even for an senior, it's a bit
much when your opponent is the Moon.

366
00:19:57,440 --> 00:19:59,320
I see.

367
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,620
I wonder if Ryo-chan is all right.

368
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:05,560
Yeah, I'm tired of
searching for diamonds now.

369
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,240
And I'm getting hungry too.

370
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:09,720
I wonder if there's a
convenience store around here.

371
00:20:11,880 --> 00:20:12,860
What's that?

372
00:20:12,860 --> 00:20:15,780
It's the lunar rover used
in the Apollo program.

373
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:18,240
They just left it behind? What a waste.

374
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:21,840
It still runs. This is great.

375
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,420
But there's no food here, is there.

376
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:27,940
It's a spacecraft.

377
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:32,340
So someone besides Apollo
came to the Moon too?

378
00:20:33,220 --> 00:20:34,120
Here goes.

379
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:36,080
Well, this is a classic.

380
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:39,780
This is an oxygen maintenance unit.

381
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:43,160
Yes, space food!

382
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,380
There are even plant seeds for
experiments and water left over.

383
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:49,740
With this, we'll manage somehow on food.

384
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:53,800
But rather than forcing ourselves to
travel all the way back over that distance,

385
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:56,300
maybe staying on the
Moon is the right choice.

386
00:20:57,940 --> 00:21:00,380
I hear ordinary people will
be coming to the Moon too, so.

387
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:01,200
Right.

388
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:03,940
As the first resident of the Moon,

389
00:21:03,940 --> 00:21:05,420
I'll claim ownership of this Moon.

390
00:21:05,420 --> 00:21:06,340
It's decided.

391
00:21:07,900 --> 00:21:09,660
Before the real estate agents get here,

392
00:21:09,660 --> 00:21:10,860
let's sell off the lots.

393
00:21:10,860 --> 00:21:11,780
First come, first served!

394
00:21:11,780 --> 00:21:14,560
First, let's build a
launch pad for spaceships.

395
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:16,820
City planning is all about the beginning.

396
00:21:16,820 --> 00:21:19,040
This will be the center of the Moon,
after all.

397
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:21,780
All the roads will be huge,
five lanes in each direction,

398
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:22,620
highways.

399
00:21:22,620 --> 00:21:24,660
There won't be traffic
jams for a hundred years.

400
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:29,280
Without plants it's too bleak.

401
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:31,700
We'll carve out the rock
and make it look the part.

402
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:34,640
Let's write the company
name in big letters too.

403
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:38,260
The day this becomes a second
Denen-chō isn't far off.

404
00:21:42,300 --> 00:21:43,300
What is this?

405
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:46,920
Is this really the Moon?

406
00:21:46,920 --> 00:21:48,640
It's a Dutch windmill!

407
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:50,660
Pyramids and a Sphinx!

408
00:21:50,660 --> 00:21:51,660
The Kremlin Palace.

409
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,620
And the Paris outer line too.

410
00:21:54,660 --> 00:22:02,360
It's here! Amazing, anyway, we've landed! So the
photos from the lunar probe were right after all.

411
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:04,820
But who on earth would
do something like this?

412
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:11,200
What does
"Ryotsu Real Estate" written over there mean? It means exactly what it says.

413
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:20,260
People barging onto private property... It's been three months since then,
and Senpai still hasn't come back.

414
00:22:20,260 --> 00:22:22,780
He can't just come back that easily.

415
00:22:22,780 --> 00:22:25,300
We don't even know if he's alive or dead.

416
00:22:26,780 --> 00:22:29,060
Everyone's running news about the Moon.

417
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:33,820
Because the Moon's surface changed shape,
the survey team went to the Moon several times,

418
00:22:33,820 --> 00:22:36,060
and each time they went missing.

419
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:39,860
Images from the third survey team,
which solve the mystery, have been sent in.

420
00:22:40,580 --> 00:22:43,320
A mysterious creature is captured
on one of the survey team's cameras.

421
00:22:43,960 --> 00:22:45,100
Please look at the upper left.

422
00:22:46,140 --> 00:22:49,220
Then the creature suddenly
lunges at the survey team.

423
00:22:50,260 --> 00:22:53,400
Two seconds later, the camera was
destroyed and the image vanished.

424
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:55,100
Chief, no way!

425
00:22:55,300 --> 00:22:56,080
Uuuugh...

426
00:22:56,480 --> 00:23:00,280
And now, we'll hear from
Professor Ezaki at the Space Center.

427
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:03,320
Yes, Professor Ezaki.

428
00:23:03,860 --> 00:23:06,860
From what I can see,
it's a creature extremely close to humans.

429
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:10,500
But I judge its intelligence to
be low and its temperament savage.

430
00:23:10,980 --> 00:23:12,380
Well, that's rich coming from you.

431
00:23:13,020 --> 00:23:13,380
Thank you very much.

432
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:15,290
Also,

433
00:23:15,340 --> 00:23:19,400
a black notebook-like object, believed to have been
dropped by the mysterious creature, has been found,

434
00:23:20,260 --> 00:23:22,340
and analysis is proceeding at a rapid pace.

435
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:25,040
That's a police notebook, you know.

436
00:23:25,040 --> 00:23:26,340
It really is Senpai.

437
00:23:26,340 --> 00:23:27,220
Ryo-chan!

438
00:23:27,220 --> 00:23:28,740
That idiot...

439
00:23:29,220 --> 00:23:31,920
Welcome, everyone on Earth!

440
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:33,460
Your voice is too quiet.

441
00:23:33,460 --> 00:23:34,440
Once more!

442
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:35,180
Yes.

443
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:38,080
Welcome, everyone on Earth!

444
00:23:38,080 --> 00:23:41,140
Welcome, everyone on Earth!

445
00:23:41,140 --> 00:23:44,280
For your stay, choose the Ryotsu Hotel!

446
00:23:44,280 --> 00:23:47,440
For your stay, choose the Ryotsu Hotel!

447
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:50,380
For all your car needs, call Ryotsu Taxi!

448
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:56,360
For your shopping,
visit Ryotsu Department Store!

449
00:23:59,060 --> 00:24:01,720
Welcome to Planet Ryotsu!

450
00:24:04,660 --> 00:24:07,000
Chief, don't go so far away!

451
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:09,060
Come, come, this way, closer, closer!

452
00:24:09,060 --> 00:24:11,660
Stay away, stay away,
come here, don't get closer!

453
00:24:11,660 --> 00:24:13,800
Back away, come, come, stop, fall back!

454
00:24:13,800 --> 00:24:16,600
Don't move, stop, help,
do something about it!

455
00:24:17,440 --> 00:24:20,000
Next time, absolutely,
the farthest frontier explained!

456
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,060
Chief!

457
00:24:47,440 --> 00:24:49,780
Decided, and inspiration strikes!

458
00:24:49,780 --> 00:24:52,700
Bouncing along, gathering it all together,

459
00:24:52,700 --> 00:24:55,660
into action, soaring away!

460
00:24:56,500 --> 00:25:00,380
A power more amazing than anything,

461
00:25:00,380 --> 00:25:06,340
if we gather everyone and come here,

462
00:25:07,260 --> 00:25:12,620
the final energy, like a dream.

463
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:20,000
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday,
painting the cosmos, standing on the ground.

464
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:23,780
The star of Kameari spun
around and traced a circle.

465
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:27,460
This should be good enough, right?

466
00:25:27,460 --> 00:25:28,920
Like hell it is!

467
00:25:42,620 --> 00:25:43,720
Thank you for watching.

